<header><p class="st-kicker">county · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Earldom of Ormond</h1><p class="st-meta">1328 CE – 1716 CE · capital Kilkenny</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The great Butler lordship of Kilkenny and Tipperary, for four centuries one of Ireland's most powerful Anglo-Irish dynasties and a loyal crown ally.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/butler-dynasty">Butlers</a> descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theobald-walter">Theobald Walter</a>, who came to Ireland with Prince John in 1185 and held the hereditary office of butler of Ireland. In 1328 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-butler-1st-earl-of-ormond">James Butler</a> became the first Earl of Ormond and was granted palatine rights over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-tipperary">Tipperary</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The earls ruled their palatinate from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilkenny-castle">Kilkenny Castle</a>, bought in 1391, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carrick-on-suir">Carrick-on-Suir</a>, with their own courts. Generally loyal to the crown, they were rivals of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kildare">Kildare</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/earldom-of-desmond">Desmond FitzGeralds</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-butler-10th-earl-of-ormond">Thomas Butler</a>, the 10th Earl, helped crush the Desmond rebellions; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-butler-1st-duke-of-ormonde">James Butler, 1st Duke of Ormonde</a>, was Lord Lieutenant under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-england">Charles II</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-butler-1st-earl-of-ormond">James Butler</a>, 2nd Duke, joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacobitism">Jacobites</a> and was attainted in 1715, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-tipperary">Tipperary</a> palatinate was abolished in 1716. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/butler-dynasty">Butlers</a> kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilkenny-castle">Kilkenny Castle</a> until 1967.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="county, 1328 CE – 1716 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">county</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:86.13%;width:7.72%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1328 CE – 1716 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kilkenny</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>James Butler, 1st Earl of Ormond, Thomas Butler, 10th Earl of Ormond, James Butler, 1st Duke of Ormonde</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity; Catholic, later Protestant earls</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Palatinate of Tipperary, Butler lordship</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1522&amp;focus=earldom-of-ormond" aria-label="Earldom of Ormond on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4518 362 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Earldom of Ormond lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4838 618L4861 599M4838 618L4861 599"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4861 599h0M4861 599h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4838 618h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4838 618h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kilkenny. <a href="/atlas?year=1522&amp;focus=earldom-of-ormond">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

